  "question": {
    "text": "Identify the pair of physical quantities that have same dimensions:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Velocity gradient and decay constant",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Angular frequency and angular momentum",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Wave number and Avogadro number",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Wein&#39;s constant and Stephan&#39;s constant",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Decay constant is measured per unit time,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>So, its dimension is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#955;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></math></p><p>We know velocity gradient&nbsp;is defined as rate of change in velocity per unit of distance. So, dimension of velocity gradient is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
